[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Kernel Object Inspection
REQ_PREFIX: ZEP-SRS-35-

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: software_requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-1
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Associating a kernel object with its type
STATEMENT: >>>
Where kernel object inspection is enabled, the Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to associate a kernel object with its object type.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-8
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Registering a kernel object for discovery
STATEMENT: >>>
Where kernel object inspection is enabled, the Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to register a kernel object associated with an object type so that it is reported when iterating over the objects of that type.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-9
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Reporting statically defined kernel objects
STATEMENT: >>>
Where kernel object inspection is enabled for a kernel object type, the Zephyr RTOS shall report the statically defined objects of that type during iteration without requiring run-time registration.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-10
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Kernel objects in stack storage
STATEMENT: >>>
If a kernel object being registered for discovery is located in a thread stack or in an interrupt stack, then the Zephyr RTOS shall not register the object.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-11
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Registration capacity exhausted
STATEMENT: >>>
If the capacity for kernel objects registered at run time is exhausted, then the Zephyr RTOS shall not register the object being registered.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-2
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Unregistering a kernel object from inspection
STATEMENT: >>>
Where kernel object inspection is enabled, the Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to unregister a previously registered kernel object.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-12
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Unregistering kernel objects in a memory range
STATEMENT: >>>
Where kernel object inspection is enabled, the Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to unregister all registered kernel objects located in a given memory range.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-13
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Unregistering kernel objects in released memory
STATEMENT: >>>
Where eviction of kernel objects on memory release is enabled, the Zephyr RTOS shall unregister registered kernel objects located in memory released by a kernel memory allocator.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-3
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Finding a kernel object type
STATEMENT: >>>
Where kernel object inspection is enabled, the Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to obtain a reference to a registered kernel object type.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-14
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Kernel object type not found
STATEMENT: >>>
If no kernel object type with the requested type identifier exists, then the Zephyr RTOS shall indicate that the type was not found.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-4
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Iterating over kernel objects of a type
STATEMENT: >>>
Where kernel object inspection is enabled, the Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to iterate over all registered kernel objects of a given object type, invoking a caller-supplied function for each object.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-15
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Iterating without synchronization
STATEMENT: >>>
Where kernel object inspection is enabled, the Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to iterate over the registered kernel objects of a given object type without synchronizing with concurrent registration changes, during which such changes may or may not be reflected.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-16
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Stopping an iteration early
STATEMENT: >>>
If the caller-supplied function invoked during an iteration over kernel objects returns a non-zero value, then the Zephyr RTOS shall stop the iteration and return that value to the caller.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-17
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Associating statistics storage with a kernel object
STATEMENT: >>>
Where kernel object statistics are enabled, the Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to associate caller-provided statistics storage with a kernel object.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-18
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Removing statistics storage from a kernel object
STATEMENT: >>>
Where kernel object statistics are enabled, the Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to remove the statistics storage association from a kernel object.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-5
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Querying kernel object statistics
STATEMENT: >>>
Where kernel object statistics are enabled, the Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to query the run-time statistics associated with a registered kernel object.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-19
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Querying raw kernel object statistics
STATEMENT: >>>
Where kernel object statistics are enabled, the Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to retrieve the unprocessed statistics data associated with a registered kernel object.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-6
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Enabling kernel object statistics
STATEMENT: >>>
Where kernel object statistics are enabled, the Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to enable statistics collection for a registered kernel object.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-20
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Disabling kernel object statistics
STATEMENT: >>>
Where kernel object statistics are enabled, the Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to disable statistics collection for a registered kernel object.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-7
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Resetting kernel object statistics
STATEMENT: >>>
Where kernel object statistics are enabled, the Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to reset the run-time statistics associated with a registered kernel object.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-21
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Unsupported statistics operation
STATEMENT: >>>
If a statistics operation is requested on a kernel object whose object type does not support that operation, then the Zephyr RTOS shall return an error indicating the operation is not supported.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-22
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Statistics operation without associated storage
STATEMENT: >>>
If a statistics operation that requires associated statistics storage is requested on a kernel object that has none, then the Zephyr RTOS shall return an error.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-35-23
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Kernel Object Inspection
TITLE: Statistics storage size mismatch
STATEMENT: >>>
If the size of the caller-provided statistics storage does not match the size defined for the object type, then the Zephyr RTOS shall return an error indicating an invalid argument.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-40
